course: dictionary
lesson: 11852
title: Words that name a job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A boatman is a man whose job is to row, sail or look after boats. He might carry people across water, or hire boats out to others. The word is made of two parts you know, boat and man, and together they tell you the job.
explain: «The boatman rowed us across the lake before the rain started.» The clues are rowed and across the lake, so a boatman works with a boat on water. Check by swapping your meaning in: "The man who looks after boats rowed us across the lake" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Boatmen have worked on rivers and canals for hundreds of years, carrying people and goods. In stories and myths, a boatman often ferries travellers across a river to the other side.
fact: A boatman is a man whose job is to row, sail or look after boats.
fact: A boatman can also be a person who hires out boats, such as on a park lake.
fact: Boatmen often carry people across water in a boat.
fact: In Greek myth, Charon is a boatman who carries the dead across the River Styx.
fact: The plural of boatman is boatmen.
exercise: «The boatman rowed the family across the river.» What is a boatman? | A boat that carries only goods | A bird that lives near water | A fish that swims in rivers | *A man whose job is to row or look after boats
exercise: Ben works at the park lake. He is a boatman who hires out boats. What does hires out mean? | *Rents them to people for a time | Builds them from wood | Sinks them in the lake | Paints them bright colours
exercise: In the Greek myth, Charon is a boatman. Who does he carry across the River Styx? | Logs of wood | Friendly dolphins | Sheep and goats | *The dead
test: «The boatman tied his small boat to the wooden jetty.» Find and copy the word that names a job. | wooden | tied | *boatman | jetty
test: What is the plural of boatman? | boatpeople | boatmens | boatmans | *boatmen
exam: Which sentence uses boatman correctly? | The boatman painted the sky red | *The boatman rowed the travellers across the river | The boatman ate a sandwich in his bed | The boatman sang loudly in the kitchen
